            <ArticleTitle>Coronary focal ectasia formation following percutaneous transluminal angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>124-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Focal ectasia of the right coronary artery developed following percutaneous transluminal angioplasty. Operative intervention was not deemed necessary. No restenosis was found on repeat coronary angiography. Five-yr follow-up was associated with a benign course.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
